{
 "_doc": "PUBLICATION-GUARD-1. Read by foundation/publication.py (python3 -m foundation publication --check, run by tests/foundation/test_publication.py in checks.yml). Every repository of the organization is public under USL-1.0 since 2026-11-15; this is what a public repository must keep true. spdx_baseline lists source files that predate the header rule: it only shrinks (--baseline), and a new file without the header fails. procedure is the pre-publication audit as it was run, for the next repository that is created private and published later.",
 "id": "PUBLICATION-GUARD-1",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "license_blob": "650d390828dd1f092f09a7fdb1593e4829ced803",
 "spdx": "SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Ultrastable-USL-1.0",
 "required_files": [
  "LICENSE",
  "NOTICE",
  "COMMERCIAL-TERMS.md",
  "CITATION.cff",
  "SECURITY.md"
 ],
 "source_suffixes": [
  ".js",
  ".mjs",
  ".ts",
  ".py",
  ".sh"
 ],
 "private_data": {
  "scan_suffixes": [
   ".md",
   ".json",
   ".jsonl",
   ".yml",
   ".yaml",
   ".py",
   ".js",
   ".mjs",
   ".toml",
   ".txt",
   ".html"
  ],
  "skip_paths": "^(doctrine/publication\\.json|tests/foundation/test_publication\\.py)$",
  "patterns": {
   "personal_email": "[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@(gmail|googlemail|outlook|hotmail|yahoo|icloud|proton|protonmail)\\.[a-z.]{2,}",
   "local_path": "[A-Za-z]:[\\\\/]{1,2}Users[\\\\/]{1,2}[A-Za-z0-9._-]+|/Users/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+(?=/)"
  },
  "allow": "\\.example$"
 },
 "procedure": [
  {
   "step": "mirror",
   "how": "git clone --mirror of every repository: all branches, tags and refs/pull"
  },
  {
   "step": "secrets",
   "how": "gitleaks git --log-opts=--all --redact=100 and trufflehog git --bare --only-verified; a verified hit is rotated first, then purged; a value is never printed"
  },
  {
   "step": "private-data",
   "how": "python3 -m foundation publication --history <mirror>; issue, comment and review text is exported and scanned the same way; a sample of Actions run logs too, they become public with the repository"
  },
  {
   "step": "license",
   "how": "python3 -m foundation publication --check in the repository; LICENSE and COMMERCIAL-TERMS.md are byte copies from ultrastable/license"
  },
  {
   "step": "flip",
   "how": "only after the steps above are clean; verify with an unauthenticated request"
  },
  {
   "step": "protect",
   "how": "secret scanning, push protection, Dependabot alerts, private vulnerability reporting, no force-push and no deletion on main (available on public repositories on the free plan)"
  },
  {
   "step": "date",
   "how": "tag disclosure-<date>, request a Software Heritage save, record both in docs/disclosure/<date>.json"
  },
  {
   "step": "rescan",
   "how": "repeat the secrets step on a clone made without credentials"
  }
 ],
 "facts": {
  "actions_on_private_repositories": "On 2026-11-15 GitHub Actions refused to start jobs on the private repositories (billing or spending limit; jobs end in failure with 0 steps). A red run with no steps is not a test result. The same workflows ran once the repositories were public.",
  "codeowners": "No CODEOWNERS that names a person: protected paths are guarded by automated checks (closedloop)."
 },
